A shape whose call site writes no `style` at all. Every other canvas fixture
in this directory passes one explicitly, so what the compiler binds to an
omitted struct prop has never been pinned anywhere -- and `canvasText` is
where it shows, because its font is read out of that struct field by field:
`String(style.fontSize) + "px " + style.fontFamily`.

`CanvasStyle` declares `fontSize float = 16.0` and `fontFamily string =
"sans-serif"`, so the answer has to be those. Bound to an empty struct
literal instead the two reads resolve to nothing and the page says
`ctx.font = String({}.fontSize) + "px " + {}.fontFamily`, which is `undefined`
at run time -- a font string no browser parses, on a page that still renders.

Which path supplies that answer is the point of the fixture. `shapeBody` in
passCanvas falls back to `ir.DeclaredDefault` and `substitute` in
passInlinePure falls back to `ir.ZeroExpr`, and today a shape reaches the
first because `isPrimitiveComponent` exempts a segmented tree's members from
the inliner. Removing that exemption moves every shape to the second, so this
is the fixture that says what such a move costs.

The `rect` beside it is the same question asked of a shape that reads no font:
its transparent `fill` and `stroke` defaults are what decide that nothing is
painted at all, which is why the draw function below brackets it and draws
nothing inside.

deny out/none/html/index.html `\{\}\.font` -- a member read off an empty style literal is undefined at run time; the declared default has to be bound at build time
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `CanvasStyle\{\}` -- the same claim on the other target: an empty record is not what CanvasStyle's declared defaults say

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import draw "sngl:ui/draw"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
}

component main() ui.node {
    draw.canvas(width=40px, height=20px) {
        draw.canvasText(x=1.0, y=1.0, content="hi")
        draw.rect(x=0.0, y=0.0, w=10.0, h=5.0)
    }
}

ui.window {
    main()
}
